{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/colorscheme"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color scheme of this environment.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"colorScheme","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColorScheme","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ColorSchemeO","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read this environment value from within a view to find out if OpenSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is currently displaying the view using the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme\/light","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme\/dark","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" appearance. The value that you receive depends on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether the user has enabled Dark Mode, possibly superseded by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the configuration of the current presentation’s view hierarchy."}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["@Environment(\\.colorScheme) private var colorScheme","","var body: some View {","    Text(colorScheme == .dark ? \"Dark\" : \"Light\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can set the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorScheme"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value directly,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but that usually isn’t what you want. Doing so changes the color"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scheme of the given view and its child views but "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the views"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above it in the view hierarchy. Instead, set a color scheme using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/preferredColorScheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier, which also propagates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value up through the view hierarchy to the enclosing presentation, like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a sheet or a window."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When adjusting your app’s user interface to match the color scheme,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consider also checking the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/colorSchemeContrast","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, which reflects a system-wide contrast setting that the user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"controls. For information about using color and contrast in your app,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/accessibility\/overview\/color-and-contrast\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you only need to provide different colors or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"images for different color scheme and contrast settings, do that in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your app’s Asset Catalog. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Xcode\/Asset-Management"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"colorScheme","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV11colorSchemeAA05ColorG0Ovp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"colorScheme","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColorScheme","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ColorSchemeO"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/colorScheme"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ColorScheme/light":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Light mode","type":"text"}],"title":"ColorScheme.light","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/colorscheme\/light","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"light","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme\/light","type":"topic"},"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility/overview/color-and-contrast/":{"title":"Color and Contrast","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Color and Contrast"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/accessibility\/overview\/color-and-contrast\/","url":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/accessibility\/overview\/color-and-contrast